    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 35 tests, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by another owner, returning **409 Conflict**, following the codebase's existing duplicate-telephone pattern:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (new, `rest/advice/`) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the rejected value, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` that maps it to `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409) with the same `ProblemDetail` structure used by the other 409 handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the email (which already lower-cases it), calls a new `rejectDuplicateEmail(email)` before saving. The check compares the new owner's email against every existing owner's email in lower-cased form, skips owners with no email, and never rejects a create that omits the email (email is optional).\n\nBecause emails are already stored lower-cased by `normalizeEmail`, and the comparison lower-cases existing values too, addresses differing only in case are correctly treated as duplicates.",
